MID_EV11_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_014_m01_001: Well, it's about time for me to go.
MID_EV11_014_m01_002: You're free to look around here, but be sure you get\nback to Ribeira. Don't wanna worry your folks.
MID_EV11_014_m01_003: Pop...do you really have to go? Do you really have\nto die?
MID_EV11_014_m01_004: Hahaha. I got no regrets, and it was good I got to see\nyour mom again after all this time. Hold on to that.
MID_EV11_014_m01_007: Aurora was truly something special. I've never seen\nsuch beauty.
MID_EV11_014_m01_008: Yeah, and it's pretty clear now where Cai gets\nhis mysterious grace from—his mother.
MID_EV11_014_m01_010: Nothin' left to say, I guess. You've grown up real\ngood, Cai.
MID_EV11_014_m01_013: You're blessed with true friends. That puts me\nat ease.
MID_EV11_014_m01_014: What? Ah, that's your father...always quick with a\ncompliment...
MID_EV11_014_m01_015: Castor... Ready?
MID_EV11_014_m01_016: Yep. Thanks for waiting. I'm ready. Well, take\ncare, everyone.
MID_EV11_014_m01_017: Cai... Please... Look after your mother.
MID_EV11_014_m01_018: Centurio... Are they gonna execute him\nright away?
MID_EV11_014_m01_019: As it turns out...no. The temples are about to begin\nan important celebration.
MID_EV11_014_m01_020: Unclean acts, like executions, are postponed for now.\nBut your father's time is still...
MID_EV11_014_m01_021: If you need anything, come see me in the temple.\nI'll do whatever I can.
MID_EV11_014_m01_046: <NCA>Thank him.
MID_EV11_014_m01_047: <NCB>Ask him for advice.
MID_EV11_014_m01_048: <ACA>Thank you, Centurio.
MID_EV11_014_m01_049: <ACA>Not a problem. And remember—you can come see\nme anytime at Aurora's temple.
MID_EV11_014_m01_050: <ACB>Is there... Is there anything I can do to save my dad?\nLike...anything at all?
MID_EV11_014_m01_025: <ACB>I'm afraid not, Cai. I've served the temple for a long\ntime now, and I've seen some things.
MID_EV11_014_m01_026: <ACB>But the Sovereign himself ordered Castor's execution.\nThere's nothing anyone can do about it.
MID_EV11_014_m01_027: Listen, this is purely a personal request.
MID_EV11_014_m01_028: I've never once seen Aurora look quite so happy as\nshe did earlier.
MID_EV11_014_m01_029: I'm certain she was overjoyed to see her child so\ngrown up.
MID_EV11_014_m01_030: So I hope you'll present yourself to her...to your\nmother...once in a while.
MID_EV11_014_m01_031: But if you're caught sneaking in, we won't be able to\ncover for you. So, please, be discreet.
MID_EV11_014_m01_032: Castor's...gone... Are you alright, Cai?
MID_EV11_014_m01_033: I can't believe it. My mind knows it's true.
MID_EV11_014_m01_034: But we just spoke like everything was normal, and...\nnow it's sinking in that I'll never see him again.
MID_EV11_014_m01_035: I didn't say everything I wanted to say, and now I'll\nnever get the chance.
MID_EV11_014_m01_036: Rrrr!
MID_EV11_014_m01_037: There has to be a way to save your father, Cai!
MID_EV11_014_m01_038: I can't see it right now, but I know it exists.
MID_EV11_014_m01_040: Peter and I are here for you. We can think of\nsomething together, right?
MID_EV11_014_m01_051: <NCA>Thank them.
MID_EV11_014_m01_041: Yeah. Thank you. Both of you.
MID_EV11_014_m01_042: Anyway, we came all the way to Dagsion. Let's look\naround and find something to cheer ourselves up.
MID_EV11_014_m01_043: You know...a boat from Saramis arrived in the harbor\nthis morning.
MID_EV11_014_m01_044: Their ruler is about to make her grand entrance.\nLooks like it'll be a huge procession.
MID_EV11_014_m01_045: They say these Saramis parades are quite a\nspectacle. Let's go see it together!
MID_EV11_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_015_m01_001: Tialla... What...happened?
MID_EV11_015_m01_002: Cai! Thank goodness.
MID_EV11_015_m01_036: <NCA>Remember what happened.
MID_EV11_015_m01_003: Ah, that's right. I held up the procession. And then\nthat scary-looking queen came up to me...
MID_EV11_015_m01_004: I'm sorry! I'm sorry! It was my fault!
MID_EV11_015_m01_007: It's fine. When she hit me, I moved away, so it took\nsome of the force out of the blow.
MID_EV11_015_m01_009: But she's stronger than I thought she would be.\nI dodged the worst, but I still caught some of it.
MID_EV11_015_m01_010: You...took the force out of the blow? Where did you\nlearn how to do that?
MID_EV11_015_m01_011: Pop drilled that fighting stuff into me from as far\nback as I can remember.
MID_EV11_015_m01_012: Not many people had an upbringing like yours, Cai.
MID_EV11_015_m01_013: Yeah, but it was totally normal for us.
MID_EV11_015_m01_014: Who gets to say what "normal" is anyway? I'm just\nglad you didn't get killed!
MID_EV11_015_m01_017: The queen and her people must be here for the\nHeroic Games event. It starts next month.
MID_EV11_015_m01_018: I heard they came all the way from Saramis to fight.
MID_EV11_015_m01_019: <NCA>Ask about the Heroic Games.
MID_EV11_015_m01_037: <ACA>This Heroic Games thing... What is it?
MID_EV11_015_m01_020: <ACA>Everyone in town's talking about it!
MID_EV11_015_m01_021: It's a gladiator contest dedicated to the revival of\nDagda the Great, or so I heard.
MID_EV11_015_m01_022: That's right! And if you win, the Divine Sovereign\nSolel will grant whatever request you ask of him!
MID_EV11_015_m01_023: You might ask to be a tactician in the imperial army\nor for a mountain of gold—anything you want!
MID_EV11_015_m01_025: He'll grant...any...request?
MID_EV11_015_m01_038: <NCA>Think about it.
MID_EV11_015_m01_026: Ohhh...
MID_EV11_015_m01_027: That's it!
MID_EV11_015_m01_028: We win the Heroic Games and ask Lord Solel to\nsave Pop from being executed!
MID_EV11_015_m01_029: But the best fighters from all over Dagda are going\nto fight in the games.
MID_EV11_015_m01_031: I'm with you, Cai. I'll do everything I can to help.
MID_EV11_015_m01_032: We'll win the games, save your father, and then go\nback to Ribeira together.
MID_EV11_015_m01_033: Peter, you're in on this too, right? Of course you are.
MID_EV11_015_m01_034: Why "of course"? I guess I don't have a choice.
MID_EV11_015_m01_035: But I don't feel good about it. Heroic Games?\nAww...
MID_EV11_016_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_016_m01_001: Hello! Um, excuse me, but...is this the right place?
MID_EV11_016_m01_002: Hehehe. Hello to you. Right place for what?
MID_EV11_016_m01_003: We'd like to enter the Heroic Games. Is this where\nthe fighters sign up?
MID_EV11_016_m01_005: Yeah, we already have a full roster. The deadline for\napplicants passed a while ago.
MID_EV11_016_m01_007: What? Oh, come on! You can't fit one more team in?
MID_EV11_016_m01_009: We really want to enter. We need to enter. Even if\nI'm really scared of entering.
MID_EV11_016_m01_010: Not possible. Rules are rules. Aaand maybe you\nhadn't noticed this, but...you're all children.
MID_EV11_016_m01_011: You fight, you get hurt. It's not nice to make your\nmommies and daddies worry, you know.
MID_EV11_016_m01_035: <NCA>Stand your ground.
MID_EV11_016_m01_012: There must be something you can do.
MID_EV11_016_m01_013: I only wanna fight so I can save my father's life.
MID_EV11_016_m01_014: Oh. Oh my. Well...
MID_EV11_016_m01_015: To be completely honest, we were planning to do an\nextra round of recruiting at the end of the month.
MID_EV11_016_m01_016: Applicants will need to pass a standard test though.
MID_EV11_016_m01_018: Understood! Thank you!
MID_EV11_016_m01_019: You have until noon on the last day of the month!\nDon't mess this up!
MID_EV11_016_m01_020: Hope those kids will be alright. The tournament's\ngoing to be rough.
MID_EV11_016_m01_021: Fighting to save his dad... Kinda gets me right in my\nsoft ol' heart.
MID_EV11_016_m01_023: We need to make sure we can pass that test at the\nend of the month.
MID_EV11_016_m01_024: At least we've still got a little time to strategize.
MID_EV11_016_m01_026: <NCA>Ask for suggestions.
MID_EV11_016_m01_037: What can we do to improve our chances?
MID_EV11_016_m01_030: Grandpa used to tell me stories about mercenaries.\nMaybe we can hire someone to fight with us.
MID_EV11_016_m01_031: Let's ask around and see who we can find.
MID_EV11_016_m01_032: Good idea. We can try out some different options\nbefore the test.
MID_EV11_016_m01_033: That's the key to getting into the games. And then \nwe'll win!
MID_EV11_016_m01_034: Yeah!
MID_EV11_017_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_017_m01_001: We currently have 95 applicants vying for four open\ntournament slots.
MID_EV11_017_m01_002: We'll begin the test now. The best fighters will move\non to the Heroic Games.
MID_EV11_017_m01_004: What in the world? That is one terrifying kusarik!
MID_EV11_017_m01_005: Yeah, it's twice as big as the ones back home.
MID_EV11_017_m01_006: <NCA>Suggest fighting it.
MID_EV11_017_m01_007: <NCB>Suggest riding it.
MID_EV11_017_m01_045: <ACA>Maybe...we're supposed to fight it?
MID_EV11_017_m01_008: <ACA>What?! It'll kill us! No way I can stick an arrow into\nthat thing.
MID_EV11_017_m01_009: <ACA>Relax. Kusariks' weak points are their noses. Stay\ncalm, kick it in the beezer, and it'll fall into line.
MID_EV11_017_m01_046: <ACB>Maybe...we're supposed to ride it?
MID_EV11_017_m01_010: <ACB>Oh, sure. It'll shake you off in an instant!
MID_EV11_017_m01_011: <ACB>I used to ride 'em back in the village all the time.\nI'm sure this one's no different.
MID_EV11_017_m01_012: A ferocious kusarik, captured on Evermist Plain.\nIt had already claimed the lives of at least 15 locals.
MID_EV11_017_m01_014: This test is pass-fail. You'll be judged on how well\nyou conduct yourselves against this foe.
MID_EV11_017_m01_015: Oh. Uh... That's it?
MID_EV11_017_m01_016: Goliath? The Butcher? What's a gladiator doing here?
MID_EV11_017_m01_019: Awww, him's a nice wittle kusawik. Does hims\nwanna head wub?
MID_EV11_017_m01_020: Bwahahaha! It got scared and pulled away! I'm\ngonna ace this test.
MID_EV11_017_m01_021: Hey! I got a better idea. How 'bout I fight the whole\nlot of you nobodies?
MID_EV11_017_m01_023: As a temple official, I will not allow you to just come\nin and do as you please!
MID_EV11_017_m01_025: Come on! Any tough guys wanna take a crack at the\nButcher? Let's go!
MID_EV11_017_m01_026: Bwahaha! Every last one of 'em turned tail and ran!\nWhat a buncha cowards!
MID_EV11_017_m01_027: Looks like I'm the only one who passed.
MID_EV11_017_m01_047: <NCA>Correct him.
MID_EV11_017_m01_028: Hold on, meathead. I'm still here.
MID_EV11_017_m01_031: What's this, a little ankle biter? Bwahaha!\nYou gonna take me down?
MID_EV11_017_m01_032: I'm not some scared little animal! I'll shut your dumb\nlaugh hole!
MID_EV11_017_m01_033: Yeah, sure you will. 
MID_EV11_017_m01_035: Gah! This guy's way scarier than that kusarik!
MID_EV11_017_m01_036: Cai, are you sure about this? He looks\nincredibly strong.
MID_EV11_017_m01_037: It's fine. No way we're failing here.
MID_EV11_017_m01_038: If we can't pass this test, how can we expect to win\nthe whole tournament?
MID_EV11_017_m01_039: Wait! Goliath is an arena veteran. Even the other\nfighters fear him.
MID_EV11_017_m01_040: What's up? You got somethin' to say, hon?
MID_EV11_017_m01_041: As a matter of fact, yes. I won't stand idly by while\nthe Butcher fights children.
MID_EV11_017_m01_042: I, Ultand Serowain, will fight with them. You got\nsomethin' to say, hon?
MID_EV11_017_m01_044: Hahahaha! Let's go, then! All of you at once!
MID_EV11_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_018_m01_001: Hoo! Didn't think I'd lose, but you all are strong!
MID_EV11_018_m01_003: If you still want to fight in the games, you can.\nEveryone else fled, so we've got some room.
MID_EV11_018_m01_004: No, no, no. I gave it all I had, and you beat me.\nI'm out.
MID_EV11_018_m01_006: Goliath, can I ask you something?
MID_EV11_018_m01_007: What was your request going to be, if you'd won\nthe tournament?
MID_EV11_018_m01_008: I've got this brother. Well, we're not real brothers, but\nI look up to him.
MID_EV11_018_m01_009: His life story's a real doozie. But he's a class act—\na once-in-a-lifetime friend.
MID_EV11_018_m01_010: I wanted to see if there was something I could do to\nmake his life a little better.
MID_EV11_018_m01_011: So I thought if I won the games, I could maybe help\nhim out a little.
MID_EV11_018_m01_012: You're kind of decent for a scary-lookin' old guy.
MID_EV11_018_m01_013: Heh heh heh... Quit it! You're embarrassin' me!
MID_EV11_018_m01_014: You crazy brats are somethin' else. I'll be rootin' for\nya, that's for sure.
MID_EV11_018_m01_015: Thanks! Meathead.
MID_EV11_018_m01_016: Besting the Butcher is a big deal.
MID_EV11_018_m01_017: This means we're in the games, right?
MID_EV11_018_m01_018: Yes. I can confirm that you're in command of the\nnecessary skills for participation in the games.
MID_EV11_018_m01_019: I'll sign you up as entrants right away, but...have you\ndecided on a clan name yet?
MID_EV11_018_m01_020: I haven't really thought about it. It's gotta be\nsomething meaningful.
MID_EV11_018_m01_021: It's hard to come up with something under pressure.\nWe should have thought about this before.
MID_EV11_018_m01_022: What about Ribeira Winds?
MID_EV11_018_m01_023: They start in Kashgar in the dry season, cross the\nsea, and blow from Mount Fabra to Ribeira.
MID_EV11_018_m01_024: Ribeira Winds are the strong seasonal winds that\nnurtured us, and they travel a long way, like we did.
MID_EV11_018_m01_025: Tialla, that's perfect. Let's go with that.
MID_EV11_018_m01_026: Yeah, I love it. It's so "us."
MID_EV11_018_m01_027: All done with the test?
MID_EV11_018_m01_028: Hm? What are you doing here?
MID_EV11_018_m01_029: Huh? Why are you here, Centurio?
MID_EV11_018_m01_030: Managing the Heroic Games requires many hands.\nAurora's temple is here to help.
MID_EV11_018_m01_031: I received a report that testing for the additional\nentrants was complete, so I stopped by to confirm.
MID_EV11_018_m01_032: Yeah. We're done. We're entering the games to\nsave Pop.
MID_EV11_018_m01_034: Y-you can't do that! It's far too dangerous!\nYou cannot worry Aurora!
MID_EV11_018_m01_035: Centurio...do you know him?
MID_EV11_018_m01_037: Ultand! Why didn't you stop this?
MID_EV11_018_m01_038: Perhaps I ought to be asking you that.
MID_EV11_018_m01_039: It's been a very long, very hard day, and here you are\nyelling at me?!
MID_EV11_018_m01_040: I guess neither of us could have prevented this.\nCome close. I need to tell you something.
MID_EV11_018_m01_041: What is it? Mm-hm... Mmm-hmm... Wait. WHAT?!
MID_EV11_018_m01_042: This kid is Aurora's son?!
MID_EV11_018_m01_043: Not so loud, Ultand! Why do you think I\nwhispered it?